# Custom-system setup for the "assigned_count == nfirst_neighs" GUESSFAIL
# counterexample (see fix_bond_react.cpp's make_a_guess(), ~line 1586).
#
# Unlike every other reaction in this library, the system tested here is
# NOT a verbatim copy of the pre-reaction template (crosslink.pre): it's
# one single 13-bead coarse-grained homopolymer chain, read from
# crosslink.data. Beads 5 and 9 sit 1.0 apart in SPACE but only 4 bonds
# apart on the chain's own BACKBONE. crosslink.pre's template describes
# an intermolecular crosslink between two DIFFERENT, disconnected 7-atom
# fragments (bonding atom = the middle, 4th, atom of each) -- but because
# beads 5 and 9 are so close along the very same backbone, trying to
# match each half of that template against a different side of the chain
# makes the two fragments' outward (radius-3) neighbor searches
# physically overlap on beads 6, 7, 8: a pseudo-intrachain match that's
# topologically impossible to fill (the same real atom would have to
# simultaneously be two different template atoms). This can only be
# tested against a real pre-existing system shaped like that -- inserting
# crosslink.pre as-is (like every ordinary reaction in this library does)
# would just trivially match itself, with no such ambiguity at all.
#
# Expected outcome (this is what make_a_guess()'s assigned_count check
# defends): a clean reject, zero reactions, no error. See
# bond-react-topology/README.md, "Custom systems for counterexamples".
#
# ${exampledir} is set by the test harness itself (build_system(), in
# ../test_fix_bond_react_topology.cpp) to this example's own folder, so
# crosslink.data can be found regardless of the test binary's actual
# working directory.

units          lj
dimension      3
boundary       p p p
atom_style     molecular

read_data      ${exampledir}/crosslink.data &
               extra/special/per/atom 30 extra/bond/per/atom 2

pair_style     zero 2.0
pair_coeff     * *

bond_style     zero
bond_coeff     *

special_bonds  lj 0.0 0.0 0.0

velocity       all set 0.0 0.0 0.0
